      "accordion_parsys1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "accPosId": 1,
        "cols2_2_3_1_3": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:16:41 GMT-0400",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:16:41 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
          "col1": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "text": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:16:50 GMT-0400",
              "text": "<p>Non-clinical testing and analysis have demonstrated that when used in the neurovasculture, Stryker Detachable Coils are MR Conditional. A patient with Stryker Detachable Coils can be safely scanned immediately after placement of the coils, under the following conditions:<br>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Static magnetic field of 1.5 or 3.0 Tesla</li>\n<li>Spatial gradient field up to 2500 Gauss/cm (25 Tesla/m)</li>\n<li>Normal operational mode for gradients and SAR (maximum whole body&nbsp;averaged specific absorption rate (SAR) of lower than 2.0 W/kg and maximum&nbsp;head SAR of lower than 3.2 W/kg) for a total active MR scan time (with RF&nbsp;exposure) of 15 minutes or less per scan sequence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In an analysis based on the temperature rises in non-clinical testing of spherical aneurysm models, the Detachable Coils were determined to produce an in-vivo temperature rise of&nbsp;2°C or less for 15 minutes of MR scanning in normal mode operation in 1.5 T and 3 T MR systems. The Detachable Coils should not migrate in this MRI environment.</p>\n<p>Temperature testing was not conducted in arteriovenous malformations or fistulae models. MR image quality may be compromised if the area of interest is in the same area or relatively close to the position of the device. Therefore, it may be necessary to optimize MR imagining parameters for the presence of this implant.&nbsp;<br>\n</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Sep 18 2025 17:24:34 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "accordion_parsys2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "accPosId": 2,
        "cols2_2_3_1_3": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:28:14 GMT-0400",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:28:14 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
          "col1": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "text": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:28:18 GMT-0400",
              "text": "<p>Non-clinical testing and analysis have demonstrated that when used in peripheral vasculature Stryker Detachable Coils are MR Conditional. A patient can be safely scanned immediately after placement of the coils, under the following conditions:<br>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Static magnetic field of 1.5 and 3.0 Tesla</li>\n<li>Spatial gradient field up to 2500 Gauss/cm (25 Tesla/m)</li>\n<li>Normal operational mode for gradients and SAR (maximum whole body averaged&nbsp;specific absorption rate (SAR) of lower than 2.0 W/kg and maximum head SAR of&nbsp;lower than 3.2 W/kg) for a total of active MR scan time (with RF exposure) of 15&nbsp;minutes or less per scan sequence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In an analysis based on the temperature rises in non-clinical testing of a bundle of 30 test coils with a length of 109mm and the calculated SAR in the patient during MR scan, the test coils were determined to produce an in-vivo temperature rise of 7.4°C or lower for 15 minutes of MR scanning in normal operational mode in 1.5 T and 3 T MR systems. The Detachable Coils should not migrate in this MRI environment. The SAR limit of 2 W/kg applies only for coil placement in the torso. A reduction of SAR limits may be appropriate for coil placement in the legs or arms.</p>\n<p>MR image quality may be compromised if the area of interest is in the same area or relatively close to the position of the device. Therefore, it may be necessary to optimize MR imaging parameters for the presence of this implant.</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Sep 23 2025 14:57:38 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "accordion_parsys3": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "accPosId": 3,
        "cols2_2_3_1_3": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:47:43 GMT-0400",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:47:43 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
          "col1": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "text": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:47:48 GMT-0400",
              "text": "<p>Non-clinical testing and analysis have demonstrated that Neuroform Stent is MR Conditional alone, or when overlapped with a second stent, and adjacent to a Stryker Neurovascular coil mass. A patient with Neuroform Stent can be safely scanned immediately after placement of this implant, under the following conditions:<br>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Static magnetic field of 1.5 and 3.0 Tesla</li>\n<li>Spatial gradient field up to 2500 Gauss/cm (25 Tesla/m)</li>\n<li>Normal operational mode for gradients and SAR (maximum whole body averaged specific&nbsp;absorption rate (SAR) of lower than 2.0 W/kg and maximum head SAR of lower than 3.2 W/kg) for a total active MR scan time (with RF exposure) of 15 minutes or less per scan&nbsp;sequence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In an analysis based on the temperature rises in non-clinical testing of stents and the calculated SAR in the patient during an MR scan, Neuroform Stents were determined to product an in-vivo temperature rise of 4.0<sup>o</sup>C or lower for 15 minutes of MR scanning in normal operational mode in 1.5 T and 3 T MR systems. The Neuroform Stent should not migrate in this MRI environment.</p>\n<p>MR image quality may be compromised if the area of interest is in the same area or relatively close to the position of the device.</p>\n<p>In Spin Echo and Gradient Echo sequence evaluations Neuroform stent image artifact extended approximately 2mm from the device. Lumen of the stent was partially obscured by the artifact. Therefore, it may be necessary to optimize MR imaging parameters for the presence of this implant.<br>\n</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 24 2017 15:09:57 GMT-0400",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          }
        },
