      "accordion_parsys6": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "accPosId": 6,
        "cols2_2_3_1_3": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:54:54 GMT-0400",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:54:54 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
          "col1": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "text": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-5b105250fc@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Tue Oct 24 2017 14:54:59 GMT-0400",
              "text": "<p>Non-clinical testing and analysis have demonstrated the Target Detachable Coils&nbsp;are MR Conditional. A patient with this device can be safely scanned immediately&nbsp;after placement of the coils in an MR system meeting the following conditions:<br>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Static magnetic field of 3.0 T or less</li>\n<li>Maximum spatial gradient magnetic field of 2500 gauss/cm (25 T/m)</li>\n<li>Maximum MR system reported, head specific absorption rate (SAR) &lt; 3.2 W/kg&nbsp;and whole body averaged SAR &lt; 1 W/kg (Normal operating mode)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Under the scan conditions defined above, the Target Detachable Coils are&nbsp;expected to produce a maximum temperature rise of less than 2°C after 15 minutes of continuous scanning.</p>\n<p>In non-clinical testing, the image artifact caused by the device extends&nbsp;approximately 13 mm from the Target Detachable Coils when imaged with a&nbsp;gradient echo pulse sequence and a 3.0 T MRI system.</p>\n<p>Target Detachable Coils are made from non-magnetic platinum-tungsten alloy and&nbsp;should not migrate in the magnetic field. The health state of the patient or the&nbsp;presence of other implants may require reduction of the MRI limits.<br>\n</p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Sep 18 2025 17:26:46 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          }
        },
